# 1v1, cloud locks to the PC (BENCH-253), round 14: RAM-18 escape-bend lines on 11 rammers (box L, 21 Nov), plus the
# ScalpBotC ram-flee line that round 13 never read (its PC panel lost the line; coverage/shards/dzlane/B/scalpbotc-jar.md).
# Cloud locks (master + RAM-18, Robocode 1.12.0, live turn time; coverage/shards/dzlane/L/rclass/close-diag.md, locks.tsv):
#   rbd (RAM-18 escape bend): a CLASS lock on the 11, 12 fresh seeds 79700: pooled +1.85 +- 0.60 against c and
#      +1.83 +- 0.65 against an A/A twin (score points a robot); 6-seed screen 79600 +1.74 / +1.69. Per robot, the smaller
#      of the reads against c and aa: Impact +3.19, Kowari +2.69, GrubbmThree +2.32, Sanguijuela +2.20, NanoDeath +2.22,
#      Bicephal +1.90, UbaRamLT +1.64, Leopard +0.78, PureAggression +0.65, Sabreur +0.61, MaxRisk +0.36. Machete (-0.7)
#      left out.
#   rf (RAM-15 ram-flee): ScalpBotC +1.22 (low +0.76, 24 seeds, box B 72310-21 + 72330-41).
#   livematch  the released jar and BeepBoop 2.0 on the 31-robot panel at the live constant, read against live
#   lock       panel-locks.txt  c / aa / rbd / rf, 12 fresh seeds from 85000, --cpu-constant live, in work/pc-locks14
#              (earlier rounds' battles stay in work/pc-locks to -locks13)
#   gate       each robot judged on its own arm only (lock_prep.py --restrict); it keeps its line where the 95% low end
#              is above 0 (mode_table.py --margin 0). The rbd pooled read over the 11 is in the -lock.md report too.
# Before starting, check on the PC that `grep -c ScalpBotC panel-locks.txt` prints 1.
# Leigh starts it once the PC is free (one card at a time, from master):
#   git checkout master && git pull
#   .\queue.ps1 run pc-locks --fresh        (or  ./queue.sh run pc-locks --fresh)
#   --fresh because round 13 left this plan's queue state marked complete; an interrupted round 14 resumes without it.
# One bench queue, RoboRumble workers at 0, 16 workers, truth log off. 576 lock battles (12 robots, 4 arms, 12 seeds), about
# 20 minutes with the live-match check.
#
# Why it should win (the PC card rule of 2026-11-03):
#   - Per-opponent tailoring: every line names one robot; every other robot, team and melee play bit for bit as master
#     (RAM-18 only acts inside RAM-2's rammer escape, in a duel, against a robot the table names).
#   - Diagnosis first (truth logs of master and BeepBoop 2.0 against 14 rammers, 4 seeds 78600, 20-21 Nov): the rammers'
#     shots under 150 px hit us 49% of the time and BeepBoop 25% (same power 2.7), about 2x at every range. Replaying
#     each bullet against the real path: head-on aim would hit both 15%, LINEAR aim would hit us 32% and BeepBoop 10%.
#     We run dead straight at full speed through 25% of those flights (BeepBoop 3%; it flees on curves), heading away,
#     because RAM-2's escape drives fixed absolute headings, which is the path a linear aim leads. RAM-5/14/17 only
#     weigh shots already in flight; rh/rcl/rfn and MOVE-47 steady orbit were level or worse on this panel.
#   - The fix is the mechanism: for 10 ticks after each shot, the escape leaves out headings within 25 degrees of the
#     line we were on when it fired. On the cloud it cut linear exposure under 150 px from 32% to 18% and the rammers'
#     close hit rate from 51% to 43% (truth-logged screen), and held a 12-seed class lock against both twins.
#   - ScalpBotC charges us (box B charge census); ram-flee backs away from a charger within 200 px, as on the 13 rf
#     robots round 13 banked.
# Stop rules (docs/bench/watch.md): the watcher's A/A rule needs 10 robots read in both c and aa, which this lock reaches
# only late, so no aa stop rule is set; aa is read in the gate (multiarm.py prints aa against c). The lock halts on 30 failed
# battles, an arm scoring nothing in 8, 60+ skipped turns a battle over the last 24 or no battle in 30 minutes. The
# live-match step stops the card if the PC no longer scores us and BeepBoop as live does (tools/live_match.py exit 3).
# ALERT opens an issue for Leigh on any stop.
# Bank: the owning cloud thread adds the gate's lines on this card's results PR. Nothing is released by the card.
set V = 3.23
set P = --parallel 16 --no-truth-log --failed-ok
set C = --skip-build --skip-fetch --rounds 35 --cpu-constant live --child-heap 2G
set W = work/pc-locks14
set OUT = ../docs/bench/local
set ALERT = lgriffin

prep | git checkout -q master && mkdir -p bisect work && (cd .. && mvn -q -DskipTests package) && cp ../hadur-robot/target/hadur117.Hadur_${V}.jar bisect/ && bash ./build-ablation.sh aa && python3 tools/lock_prep.py plans/locks-pick.tsv panel-locks.txt plans/pc-locks.arms ${W}-prep && bash ${W}-prep/build.sh && for a in rbd rf; do test -f bisect/hadur117.Hadur_${V}$a.jar || exit 1; done && bash tools/fetch_live_jar.sh && ./fetch-opponents.sh --set panel-r31.txt && ./fetch-opponents.sh --set livematch-bb.txt && test -f opponents/kc.mega.BeepBoop_2.0.jar && ./fetch-opponents.sh --set panel-locks.txt && mvn -q compile

livematch | ./bench-top20.sh ${C} ${P} --set panel-r31.txt --seeds 2 --seed-base 21700 --arms plans/livematch.arms --out work/pc-livematch-rel-live --label pc-locks-livematch --shuffle-jobs && python3 tools/live_match.py work/pc-livematch-rel-live/arms.tsv --out ${OUT}/pc-locks14-livematch.md
  after: prep
  watch: field=1217
  stop: fails 30
  stop: dead 8
  stop: stall 30m

lock | ./bench-top20.sh ${C} ${P} --set panel-locks.txt --seeds 12 --seed-base 85000 --arms ${W}-prep/lock.arms --out ${W} --label pc-locks --shuffle-jobs
  after: livematch
  watch: field=1217
  stop: fails 30
  stop: dead 8
  stop: skips 60 over 24
  stop: stall 30m

gate | python3 ../data/tools/multiarm.py ${W}/arms.tsv --out ${OUT}/$(date +%Y-%m-%d)_pc-locks14-lock.md && python3 tools/lock_prep.py --restrict ${W}/arms.tsv ${W}-prep ${W}/arms-picked.tsv && python3 ../data/tools/mode_table.py ${W}/arms-picked.tsv --margin 0 --out-tsv ${OUT}/pc-locks14-lock-pick.tsv --out ${OUT}/$(date +%Y-%m-%d)_pc-locks14-lock-pick.md && python3 tools/per_robot.py ${W}/arms-picked.tsv --arms rbd rf --out ${OUT}/$(date +%Y-%m-%d)_pc-locks14-lock-per-robot.md --out-tsv ${OUT}/pc-locks14-lock-per-robot.tsv
  after: lock

pr | bash tools/open_results_pr.sh claude/pc-locks14-results "1v1 cloud locks, round 14 (11 robots on rbd, 1 on rf) locked on 12 fresh PC seeds" ${OUT}/pc-locks14-livematch.md ${OUT}/*_pc-locks14-*.md ${OUT}/pc-locks14-lock-per-robot.tsv $(find ${OUT} -maxdepth 1 -name 'pc-locks14-lock-pick.tsv' -size +0c)
  after: gate
